1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,900
Number four will keep you up tonight.

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:03,200
Number one.

3
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:06,350
Most of Earth's volcanoes
are hidden underwater.

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,250
Almost every eruption happens
on the ocean floor, unseen.

5
00:00:10,850 --> 00:00:11,550
Number two.

6
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:14,050
Volcanic ash is not soft.

7
00:00:14,650 --> 00:00:16,900
It's tiny shards
of rock and glass,

8
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,000
sharp enough to destroy
a jet engine.

9
00:00:19,650 --> 00:00:20,400
Number three.

10
00:00:21,050 --> 00:00:23,900
Lightning can form inside
a volcano's ash cloud.

11
00:00:24,550 --> 00:00:25,300
Number four.

12
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:28,950
In 1815, Tambora threw up
so much ash

13
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,100
that the next year
had almost no summer.

14
00:00:31,750 --> 00:00:32,900
It snowed in June.

15
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:34,200
Number five.

16
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:38,400
Mauna Loa in Hawaii is the largest
active volcano on Earth,

17
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,900
and most of it is hidden
under the sea.

18
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:43,250
Follow Fact Arcana for more.

